 4. 🏍️ Barely a LiveWire 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 A LiveWire S2 Alpinista electric motorcycle. Photo: Courtesy of LiveWire

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 LiveWire, the electric motorcycle maker spun off from Harley-Davidson, is hanging on by a drive belt.

 Shares skidded 43.7% today to under $1 after the company warned it may not survive the next year. 🪫 The big picture: The company — spun off from Harley in 2022 with visions of pioneering the future of motorcycling — is burning cash and selling few bikes.

 It sold 241 electric motorcycles in the September quarter, generating just $2.7 million in revenue. It generated almost twice as much in sales selling electric balance bikes and bicycles. Altogether, the company posted an $18.6 million net loss for the quarter on $7.9 million of revenue, and ended September with $40 million in cash — less than half of what it had at the start of the year. 🗣️ What's next: LiveWire said it "continues to evaluate and pursue comprehensive financing and other strategic alternatives, which may include significant capital raises, strategic partnerships or investments, sales, and other strategic transactions."

 
 
